1
00:00:01,830 --> 00:00:04,000
弗里曼: 我们生活在真实的世界中吗？
Freeman: Do we live in the real world?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,630
[闹钟响]
[ Alarm clock beeps ]

3
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:07,770
还是一切都只存在于我们思维中？
Or is it all in our minds?

4
00:00:07,770 --> 00:00:11,810
宇宙就是我们看到的那样吗？
Do we see the universe as it is?

5
00:00:11,810 --> 00:00:14,240
还是我们的感觉欺骗了我们？
Or do our senses deceive us?

6
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:20,580
科学观测揭示了隐藏的现实。
Scientific observation reveals hidden realities.

7
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:24,180
我们的感觉判断并不可信。
The judgment of our senses cannot be trusted.

8
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:25,390
[引擎启动]
[ Engine revs ]

9
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:30,630
我们对生命和宇宙的基本设想
And our basic assumptions about life and the universe

10
00:00:30,630 --> 00:00:31,990
可能都是错的。
may be false.

11
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:36,060
这种存在是幻觉吗？
Is existence an illusion?

12
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:38,800
现实是真实的吗？
Is reality real?

13
00:00:44,570 --> 00:00:49,740
空间、时间、生命本身,
Space,time,life itself.

14
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:57,550
宇宙的奥秘，尽在穿越虫洞。
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

15
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:04,560
现实是真实的吗？

16
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,500
什么才是真实？
What is real?

17
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:15,770
我们认为日常生活中碰到的一切都是真实。
We assume it's everything we encounter in our daily lives.

18
00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:17,710
但我们又如何能确定
But how can we be certain

19
00:01:17,710 --> 00:01:22,040
我们看到的宇宙就是确实存在的？
the universe we see around us actually exists?

20
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:23,980
我们又如何知道
And how can we know

21
00:01:23,980 --> 00:01:29,520
我们看到的世界,和别人对世界的看法是否一致？
that the world we see matches what anyone else experiences?

22
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:34,690
我们的感官感受确实让现实看起来足够真实。
Our senses certainly make reality seem real enough.

23
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:37,760
这些固态的东西,
These things are solid.

24
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:40,400
但是...
But...

25
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,700
假如它们其实不是呢？
What if they actually aren't?

26
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:48,640
我们认为的现实可能是一个脆弱的幻象,
Our reality may be a fragile tissue of illusions

27
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:52,570
关于我们自身,我们社会,
illusions about ourselves,our society,

28
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:56,950
甚至整个自然界都是幻象。
and even the whole of the natural world.

29
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:05,390
小时候,一个魔术师来到了我的小镇。
When I was young,a magician came to town.

30
00:02:05,390 --> 00:02:07,690
他表演的很棒。
He was pretty good.

31
00:02:07,690 --> 00:02:11,960
看着他的表演,我开始怀疑自己的双眼是否可靠,
Watching him made me doubt the reliability of my own eyes.

32
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:16,900
无论我多使劲的看,也看不透他是如何做到的。
No matter how hard I looked,I couldn't see how he did it.

33
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:19,030
我错过了什么？
What was I missing?

34
00:02:19,030 --> 00:02:23,110
而且我为什么会错过这些？
And why was I missing it?

35
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,750
Lawrence Rosenblum是
Lawrence Rosenblum is a Professor

36
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:32,250
知觉心理学领域的一名教授,
of perceptual psychology

37
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:34,980
就职于加州大学河滨分校。
at the university of California,riverside.

38
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:37,380
他同样也玩魔术。
He also dabbles in magic.

39
00:02:37,390 --> 00:02:38,990
比起大多数人,
More than most,

40
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:44,660
Larry了解魔术师扭曲现实的手段。
Larry understands the mechanisms magicians use to warp reality.

41
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:48,060
男人：女士们先生们,欢迎神奇的Larry！
Man: Ladies and gentlemen,the amazing Larry!

42
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:54,900
Rosenblum: 女士们先生们,大家晚上好。
Rosenblum: Good evening,ladies and gentlemen.

43
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:58,940
今天晚上,我要告诉你们关于认知感知的一些东西,
Tonight,I'd like to teach you a little bit about perception.

44
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:07,180
这是个什么戏法呢？
How did that trick work?

45
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:09,480
好吧,当我往上扔球的时候,
Well,as I was throwing the ball up,

46
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:12,020
你们的注意力会跟着我的视线移动,
you were following my eyes with your attention.

47
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:14,060
这一直持续到我最后一次扔球,
And that continued through the last throw,

48
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:15,360
这次其实我并没有扔。
which was not a real throw.

49
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:17,630
这种误导的手法
That technique of misdirection is just one

50
00:03:17,630 --> 00:03:20,500
只是专业魔术师用的众多手段之一。
of the many techniques that professional magicians use.

51
00:03:23,930 --> 00:03:27,470
弗里曼: 像David Gabbay这样的魔术师用到的戏法
Freeman: Illusionists like David Gabbay perform tricks

52
00:03:27,470 --> 00:03:32,570
一次又一次的欺骗了我们,无论我们离得多近进行观看。
that fool us again and again,no matter how closely we watch.

53
00:03:32,570 --> 00:03:35,210
他们利用了我们大脑想要
They take advantage of our brain's eagerness

54
00:03:35,210 --> 00:03:36,810
弄清这个世界的渴望。
to make sense of the world.

55
00:03:36,810 --> 00:03:40,150
Rosenblum: David并不为我们的大脑创造真实情况,
Rosenblum: David's not helping our brains create a reality

56
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:44,150
而是通过不同的方式引导我们
as much as guiding our attention of the perceptual information

57
00:03:44,150 --> 00:03:45,690
对知觉信息的注意。
in different ways.

58
00:03:45,690 --> 00:03:50,190
通过这种手段,我认为David可以教给我们很多东西。
And in that way,I think that David has a lot to teach us.

59
00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:53,190
弗里曼: David的手法利用了一种心理捷径,
Freeman: David's trick exploits a mental shortcut

60
00:03:53,190 --> 00:03:55,630
称为“变形完成”。
called amodal completion.

61
00:03:55,630 --> 00:03:57,400
这是它的工作原理,
Here is how it works.

62
00:03:57,400 --> 00:04:01,570
假如你看到了一只兔子,
Let's say you see a rabbit.

63
00:04:01,570 --> 00:04:05,510
接着遮住你对于兔子的部分视野,
Then your view of the rabbit is partially blocked.

64
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:07,140
那么这个兔子还在吗？
Is the rabbit still there?

65
00:04:07,140 --> 00:04:08,810
当然在。
Of course.

66
00:04:08,810 --> 00:04:11,750
你这么认为是因为你的大脑
You know that because your brain matches it up

67
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:13,950
将这个兔子的三维模型
with a three-dimensional model of a rabbit

68
00:04:13,950 --> 00:04:15,890
和你记忆中的兔子整合了起来,
you have filed in your memory.

69
00:04:15,890 --> 00:04:19,350
你的大脑补充了无法看到的部分。
Your brain fills in the missing piece.

70
00:04:19,350 --> 00:04:21,490
看！
Voilà!

71
00:04:21,490 --> 00:04:25,090
弗里曼: 我们的思维中储存着千百万个这类模型,
Freeman: We have millions of these models stored in our minds.

72
00:04:25,090 --> 00:04:26,560
我们通过这些模型
We use them to assemble

73
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:29,470
将看起来似乎是连续的世界图景
a seemingly continuous picture of the world

74
00:04:29,470 --> 00:04:33,270
组装成我们认为的真实。
what we think of as reality.

75
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:38,180
我们的真实感被我们
Our sense of reality is profoundly affected

76
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:40,780
共同工作的多种感觉深刻影响。
by the way our senses work together.

77
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:44,680
举个例子...
For instance...

78
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:48,220
Bah,bah,bah,bah...

79
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:49,390
弗里曼: 你听到了什么？
Freeman: What do you hear?

80
00:04:49,390 --> 00:04:52,050
Bah,bah,bah...

81
00:04:52,060 --> 00:04:56,930
Larry似乎一直在说“Bah,bah,bah.”
Larry seems to be saying,"Bah,bah,bah."

82
00:04:56,930 --> 00:05:02,670
但将情况稍加变化就会变成这样,
but here's what happens when the picture is changed just a bit.

83
00:05:02,670 --> 00:05:04,740
Fah,fah,fah,fah...

84
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:09,110
弗里曼: 现在听起来他就像在说“Fah,fah,fah.”
Freeman: Now it sounds like he is saying,"Fah,fah,fah."

85
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:11,440
但闭上眼再听,
but close your eyes and listen.

86
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:13,410
声音其实是没有变的。
The sound hasn't changed.

87
00:05:13,410 --> 00:05:17,680
Larry说的仍然是“Bah,” 发音是“B.”
Larry is still saying,"Bah," With a "B."

88
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:20,020
bah,bah,bah.

89
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:23,750
在这个例子中,听到“Bah”而看到“Vah”,
In the case with an auditory "Bah" And a visual "Vah,"

90
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:26,390
结果就是视觉信息
what happens is the visual information ends up

91
00:05:26,390 --> 00:05:28,530
优先于听觉信息,
overriding the auditory information

92
00:05:28,530 --> 00:05:29,930
因为视觉信息更为显著,
because it's so salient.

93
00:05:29,930 --> 00:05:31,490
看东西更容易。
It is so easy to see.

94
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:33,500
Bah,bah,bah.

95
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:35,160
而这个例子中,感知脑,
And the perceptual brain,in this case,

96
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:39,340
主要是听觉脑使用这些视觉信息
mostly the auditory brain ends up using that information

97
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:42,410
将“Bah”变得听起来更像“Vah”,
to kind of push the "Bah" to sound more like a "Vah,"

98
00:05:42,410 --> 00:05:44,240
这样就造成了人们
and that's what people end up believing

99
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,780
最终认为自己听到的信息。
they're actually hearing.

100
00:05:48,050 --> 00:05:52,020
弗里曼: 我们脑中有许多不同的感受系统相互作用,
Freeman: Many different sensory systems interact within our brains.

101
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:55,890
我们的思维获取这些信息并整理成事件,
Our minds take this information and tell a story about it.

102
00:05:55,890 --> 00:05:57,590
我们称之为现实。
We call it reality.

103
00:05:57,590 --> 00:06:01,320
我们感知的信息比我们能够意识到的多很多,
We're perceiving a lot more than we realize.

104
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,190
我之所以这么说是因为
And what I mean by that is

105
00:06:03,190 --> 00:06:05,560
所有的感知信息通道都可将信息
that there are entire channels of information

106
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:07,060
在我们的意识水平之下
that are getting to the brain

107
00:06:07,060 --> 00:06:08,970
传送到我们的脑中。
underneath our level of awareness.

108
00:06:08,970 --> 00:06:10,800
而在每一次,
But at any one time,

109
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,370
你不仅仅是在观看,
not only are you seeing something

110
00:06:12,370 --> 00:06:14,070
并集中注意力在你看的东西上,
and attending to what you're seeing,

111
00:06:14,070 --> 00:06:16,970
而你并没花精力注意的东西同样影响着你,
but what you're not attending to is affecting you as well,

112
00:06:16,970 --> 00:06:18,810
这种影响不仅仅是
and that isn't just from information

113
00:06:18,810 --> 00:06:20,080
你通过眼睛得到的信息,
you get through your eyes,

114
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,280
还有从你的耳朵、
but information you get through your ears

115
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:24,410
鼻子、皮肤得到的信息,
and through your nose and through your skin.

116
00:06:24,410 --> 00:06:27,050
所有的这些都在我们观看表演时进行着,
And all of that is happening as we're sitting there

117
00:06:27,050 --> 00:06:29,990
体验着我们认为的虚拟“现实”,
experiencing what we think is a visual reality.

118
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:32,460
其他的感觉全都对其有着影响。
The other senses are affecting it all.

119
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:37,390
弗里曼: 但对于所有的感知来说,有太多的信息我们都错过了。
Freeman: But for all we perceive,there is much we miss.

120
00:06:42,030 --> 00:06:44,840
大多数人有着同样的感知认识,
Most of us share the same set of senses.

121
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:49,740
而有一些人看事物却与旁人非常不同。
Yet some of us see things very differently than others.

122
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:53,440
我们之中会有人能够看到真实的世界吗？
Can any of us perceive the world as it truly is?

123
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:59,550
Charles Falco教授是少数可以做到的人,
Professor Charles Falco is one of the few who can.

124
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,540
他探索着不可见的世界,而其中的真实我们却都看不到。
He explores the invisible world the reality we can't see.

125
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:05,800
[相机快门声]
[ Camera shutter clicking ]

126
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:10,370
人类的视觉系统只能捕获
The human vision system only captures a really tiny fraction

127
00:07:10,370 --> 00:07:12,600
光谱中非常小的一个片段。
of the light that's available.

128
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:15,470
那么这个半身雕塑,
If we look at a bust like this,

129
00:07:15,470 --> 00:07:19,110
裸眼看就是红色的,
we see it looks red to the naked eye.

130
00:07:19,110 --> 00:07:21,640
但如果我们打上紫外光,
But if we image this in the ultraviolet,

131
00:07:21,650 --> 00:07:23,850
这个雕塑就有可能发出荧光,
possibly,this bust will fluoresce

132
00:07:23,850 --> 00:07:27,250
这是因为其中的某些化学成分。
because of some of the chemical composition that's in it.

133
00:07:27,250 --> 00:07:31,650
红外光则可以在红色染料中透过很远,
Infrared typically penetrates fairly far through red pigment.

134
00:07:31,650 --> 00:07:33,560
这样我们就能看到染料下面到底有什么,
So we'll be able to see what's underneath the pigment,

135
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:36,130
是否存在某些东西位于染料
if there's something between the pigment

136
00:07:36,130 --> 00:07:38,960
和石膏雕塑本身之间。
and the plaster bust itself.

137
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:42,870
弗里曼: 在他位于亚利桑那大学的实验室中,
Freeman: In his laboratory at the university of Arizona,

138
00:07:42,870 --> 00:07:46,740
Charles的实验设备可以用从可见光
Charles had exotic instruments that can examine objects

139
00:07:46,740 --> 00:07:48,870
到不可见光所有波长范围的光
at resolutions across all ranges

140
00:07:48,870 --> 00:07:51,470
检测物体,
of visible and invisible light

141
00:07:51,470 --> 00:07:54,740
比如X射线、紫外光、红外光等,
x-rays,ultraviolet,infrared,

142
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:57,780
这类仪器比人眼敏锐
and machines that see millions of times sharper

143
00:07:57,780 --> 00:07:59,280
上百万倍。
than human eyes.

144
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:04,250
这台电子显微镜可以看到雕塑上,看似光滑的红色染料中的
This electron microscope can read the rough molecular surface

145
00:08:04,250 --> 00:08:07,790
粗糙的分子表面。
of the bust's seemingly smooth red paint.

146
00:08:07,790 --> 00:08:11,290
而他所有“收藏品”中的御宝
The crown jewel of his collection

147
00:08:11,290 --> 00:08:14,900
是一台可以检测原子间空隙的仪器,
is a machine that reads the space between atoms,

148
00:08:14,900 --> 00:08:18,230
这可以帮助物理学家以完全不同的方式
giving physicists a completely different way

149
00:08:18,230 --> 00:08:22,410
观测分子是如何构建的。
of looking at how molecules are constructed.

150
00:08:22,410 --> 00:08:23,910
Falco: 如果你只用自己的眼睛,
Falco: If you only have your eyes,

151
00:08:23,910 --> 00:08:27,440
看一些东西,你认为你已经了解它了,
you look at something,you think you understand it.

152
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:31,480
可当你用更多的工具来观察它,
Turns out that the more tools you have to look at something,

153
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,980
你就又能得到更多的信息。
it reveals much more information.

154
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:36,990
所以真实是一个远比我们想象的
So reality is a much more complex thing

155
00:08:36,990 --> 00:08:38,320
更为复杂的东西。
than we think about.

156
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:40,890
我们用越多的手段研究真实,
The more ways we have studying of reality,

157
00:08:40,890 --> 00:08:43,690
就越能体会到真实是一个
the more we realize reality is a bigger picture

158
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:47,060
比我们能够理解的范围更宏大的图景。
than we could possibly have understood before.

159
00:08:49,830 --> 00:08:52,300
弗里曼: 并没有一种进化压力
Freeman: There is no evolutionary pressure

160
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:54,700
促使某种生物进化到可以看清现实,
to create an animal that sees reality as it really is.

161
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:59,840
我们只进化出了我们需要看到的“真实”,
We have evolved to see the reality we need to see.

162
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:03,310
当我们看到什么东西时,我们的大脑
When we see something,how our brain interprets it

163
00:09:03,310 --> 00:09:06,920
并不会按照进入我们眼球的情况进行说明,
isn't usually what exactly is imprinted on our eyeball.

164
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
我们不是摄像机,
We're not a camera.

165
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,970
我们的视网膜后面还有一个大脑,
We have a brain behind our retinas.

166
00:09:10,970 --> 00:09:14,170
这个脑可以处理信息,
And the brain processes the information

167
00:09:14,170 --> 00:09:17,370
告诉我们它想看什么。
and tells us what it wants us to see.

168
00:09:17,370 --> 00:09:19,270
我们身边的世界中
There is so much visual information

169
00:09:19,270 --> 00:09:22,210
有太多的视觉信息,
in the world around us that it turns out

170
00:09:22,210 --> 00:09:25,150
而大脑给了我们有限的注意焦点,
our brain gives us a limited spotlight of attention,

171
00:09:25,150 --> 00:09:28,550
这样我们就能集中注意力于我们面前的事情,
where we focus our attention on exactly what's in front of us,

172
00:09:28,550 --> 00:09:31,750
忽略掉其他地方正在发生的事。
ignoring things that go on everywhere else.

173
00:09:35,290 --> 00:09:38,590
弗里曼: 当你的注意力被什么东西吸引时,
Freeman: When your attention's attracted by something,

174
00:09:38,590 --> 00:09:40,630
神经细胞就会增强
neurons enhance the sensitivity

175
00:09:40,630 --> 00:09:43,300
你对视场中央区域的敏感性,
of the central region of your field of vision

176
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:47,540
并抑制对周围区域的敏感性。
and suppress the sensitivity of the surrounding regions.

177
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:51,980
我们就这样通过双眼看世界。
And this is how we see the world  through binoculars.

178
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:53,840
我们只能看到
We see only a tiny fraction

179
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:56,380
面前的真实的一点点片段。
of the reality that's in front of us.

180
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:58,150
有过多的感知信息,
There is so much sensory information,

181
00:09:58,150 --> 00:09:59,780
过多的视觉信息,
so much visual information

182
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:04,020
将它们全部处理实际上是不可能的。
that,in fact,it's impossible to process it all.

183
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:06,120
所以每个人的大脑、每个动物的大脑,
So everyone's brain,every animal's brain

184
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:09,330
都被进化设置为只接受
has been programmed by evolution to accept

185
00:10:09,330 --> 00:10:13,430
信息的一小部分并对其进行处理,
only a small fraction of the information and process it.

186
00:10:13,450 --> 00:10:15,520
否则就会过载。
Otherwise,there'd be total overload.

187
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:22,490
弗里曼: 但真实并不是单纯的决定于你或我是如何看世界的,
Freeman: But reality isn't defined solely by how you or I see the world

188
00:10:22,490 --> 00:10:24,560
而是我们共享的东西。
it's something we share.

189
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,160
我们靠别人的观察
We check our observations

190
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:28,760
来检验自己的观察,
against the observations of others.

191
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:31,700
如果我们在什么是真实的问题上存在分歧,
If we didn't agree on what is real and what is not,

192
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:34,000
社会就不能运作。
society couldn't function.

193
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,100
但这个人认为
But this man believes

194
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:42,040
我们共同认为的现实才是最大的幻象。
our shared reality is the greatest illusion of all.

195
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:47,200
我并不是真实的,
I am not real.

196
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:50,600
你看到的我只是屏幕上上千个发着光的
You are looking at thousands of glowing,colored dots

197
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:51,940
彩色点组成,
on a screen.

198
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:54,270
这些点的模式
The pattern of these dots changes

199
00:10:54,270 --> 00:10:56,440
在每30分之一秒后改变一次,
once every 30th of a second,

200
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:59,540
这样就创造了运动的影像。
creating the illusion of movement.

201
00:10:59,540 --> 00:11:03,150
而我也并不是现在就说着话,
And I'm not saying these words right now.

202
00:11:03,150 --> 00:11:04,750
这是录制后的影像,
This is a captured impression

203
00:11:04,750 --> 00:11:08,920
而其中我说的话都是过去发生的,
of something I said in the recent past.

204
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:10,290
真是这样吗？
Or is it?

205
00:11:10,990 --> 00:11:13,290
如果我这么做呢？
What if I did this?

206
00:11:13,290 --> 00:11:16,330
当画面上说“Live(直播)”,
You've been conditioned

207
00:11:16,330 --> 00:11:19,230
你就会依此认为
to believe that,when something says "Live,"

208
00:11:19,230 --> 00:11:21,630
这是此时此刻正在发生的。
it's really happening right now.

209
00:11:21,630 --> 00:11:24,900
我们的社会也被这些共同的信条所同步,
Our society is tied together by these shared beliefs.

210
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,660
但这是何种程度的真实？
But how much of it is real?

211
00:11:27,660 --> 00:11:32,670
有多少又是复杂精致的幻觉？
And how much is just an elaborate fantasy?

212
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,000
对于他的大半生来说,
For much of his life,

213
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:38,700
科学家兼哲学家的Jim Baggott
scientist and philosopher Jim Baggott has been haunted

214
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:43,640
都被“什么才是真实的”这一简单问题所困惑。
by a simple question what is reality?

215
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:47,840
所有的真实都是我们脑中创造出的幻象。
All reality is a fantasy created in our own heads.

216
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:50,040
我们都被禁闭于自己的思维之中,
We are locked in the prison of our own minds,

217
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:53,710
这样的结果就是,我们为自己创造了一个
and as a consequence,we have to create for ourselves

218
00:11:53,710 --> 00:11:56,020
基于我们能够接受什么的
an understanding of what reality is like

219
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:58,420
自己对于现实的理解,
on the basis of what we can absorb,

220
00:11:58,420 --> 00:12:01,190
我们能够学到什么,能够看到什么。
what we can learn,what we can see.

221
00:12:01,190 --> 00:12:04,360
[门嘎吱作响]
[ Door creaks ]

222
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:06,330
当我们用眼睛看时,
So when we see with our eyes,

223
00:12:06,330 --> 00:12:09,860
我们察觉到的并不是真实本身,
what we perceive,of course,is not reality as such.

224
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:13,170
毕竟我们的大脑只是一块
Our brains are,after all,just clumps of tissue

225
00:12:13,170 --> 00:12:17,270
重约3.5磅的粘稠组织,
weighing about 3½ pounds,with a consistency of cold porridge.

226
00:12:17,270 --> 00:12:20,610
只有当我们在意识思维中
It's only when we interpret the electrical signals

227
00:12:20,610 --> 00:12:23,610
通过脑产生的电信号
generated by our brain in our conscious mind

228
00:12:23,610 --> 00:12:26,810
才创造出了我们每个人的真实。
do we create our individual reality.

229
00:12:26,810 --> 00:12:28,310
这就引出一个问题,
That begs the question

230
00:12:28,310 --> 00:12:31,550
当这些电信号都关闭后会发生什么？
what happens when those electrical signals are shut off?

231
00:12:31,550 --> 00:12:33,690
好吧,我马上就知道答案了。
Well,I'm about to find out.

232
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:39,220
弗里曼: Jim将会关闭自己的听觉和视觉
Freeman: Jim's going to have his hearing and vision blocked out

233
00:12:39,230 --> 00:12:41,260
十五分钟,
for 15 minutes.

234
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:44,730
这种简单的消除感觉的形式
This simple form of sensory deprivation

235
00:12:44,730 --> 00:12:47,970
将他带入到另一种现实中。
sends him into an alternate reality.

236
00:12:47,970 --> 00:12:50,040
他失去了时间观念...
He loses track of time...

237
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:51,440
[闹钟响]
[ Alarm clock rings ]

238
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:55,340
...并经历了生动的幻觉。
...and experiences vivid hallucinations.

239
00:12:55,340 --> 00:12:57,580
在没有感觉输入的情况下,
In the absence of sensory input,

240
00:12:57,580 --> 00:13:01,550
Jim“制造世界的机器(脑)”创建了一个
Jim's world-making machinery manufactures a reality

241
00:13:01,550 --> 00:13:05,390
与他身体外部世界毫无联系的现实。
with no connection to the world outside his body.

242
00:13:05,390 --> 00:13:10,020
Baggott: 失去了我的两个最主要的感觉输入后,
Baggott: Deprived of two of my most important senses,

243
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:14,390
我的脑从其他感觉上勉强拼凑出了
what happens is the brain scrambles for inputs

244
00:13:14,390 --> 00:13:15,760
感觉输入。
from other senses.

245
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:19,170
嘴中的味觉就会变得敏感,
So you become very conscious of the taste in your mouth

246
00:13:19,170 --> 00:13:21,800
我躺着的床也变得坚硬。
and the hardness of this bed that I'm lying on.

247
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:25,840
我开始进入一种梦一般的朦胧状态中,
I began to drift into some dreamlike states.

248
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:27,170
但当我的眼睛
But then I became aware

249
00:13:27,170 --> 00:13:29,210
重新睁开后,
that me eyes are,in fact,wide open,

250
00:13:29,210 --> 00:13:32,480
我就完全清醒并具有清晰的意识了。
and I'm fully awake and conscious.

251
00:13:33,510 --> 00:13:35,520
弗里曼: 当你感觉被关闭了,
Freeman: When your senses are shut off,

252
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:39,950
你的脑就创造了你自己版本的现实。
your brain makes up its own version of reality.

253
00:13:39,950 --> 00:13:45,690
但根据Jim的理论,我们全都生活在一个虚假的现实中,
But according to Jim,we all live in a false reality

254
00:13:45,690 --> 00:13:48,560
一个由社会创造的充满幻象的超现实,
a hyperreality created by society,

255
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:52,230
它变得对于我们来说
filled with illusions that have become more real to us

256
00:13:52,230 --> 00:13:55,870
比起周围的物质世界更为真实。
than the physical world around us.

257
00:13:55,870 --> 00:14:01,440
我们都是这个思维共同体的一部分,
We are all part of a community of minds,

258
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:06,110
这个共同体是一个由数十亿个大脑
a world created by billions of brains working in concert

259
00:14:06,110 --> 00:14:08,180
一致工作数千年的世界。
over thousands of years.

260
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:10,780
现代的消费社会
The modern consumer society

261
00:14:10,780 --> 00:14:14,320
是我们集体思维进化出的,使我们这个物种前进的
is the latest twist our mass mind has evolved

262
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:17,320
最新形式的对真实的扭曲,
to advance the species.

263
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:20,860
金钱位于这个社会的中心,
Money lies at the heart of this society.

264
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,460
但从许多角度来说,
But in many ways,

265
00:14:22,460 --> 00:14:27,630
这才是我们所有创造中最超现实的。
it is the most hyperreal of all of our creations.

266
00:14:27,630 --> 00:14:31,470
Baggott: 这里我有一张50美元和50英镑的纸币样张,
Baggott: I have here a $50 bill and a 50£ note.

267
00:14:31,470 --> 00:14:34,910
现在的汇率告诉我们
Current currency-conversion rates tells us that the pound

268
00:14:34,910 --> 00:14:38,050
英镑的汇率是美元的1.5倍,
is about 1.5 times greater in value than the dollar.

269
00:14:38,050 --> 00:14:41,150
而这些小片纸张却像咒符一样
And these little pieces of paper hold such a spell

270
00:14:41,150 --> 00:14:42,180
主宰我们的生活,
over our lives.

271
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:44,250
它们几乎决定了
They tell us whether almost

272
00:14:44,250 --> 00:14:46,320
谁能活下去,谁将会死去。
who is gonna live,who is gonna die.

273
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,420
但价值确是
But,really,value is something

274
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:51,690
我们创造的超现实的一部分,
that's part of the hyperreality that we've created,

275
00:14:51,690 --> 00:14:54,560
而我并不知道这片由四分之三的棉纤维
and I don't know what the real value of a piece of paper

276
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:57,700
和四分之一亚麻做成的纸的真实价值,
made of three parts cotton fiber and one part linen really is,

277
00:14:57,700 --> 00:15:02,100
但我可以告诉你,它的价值绝对远小于50美元或50英镑。
but I can tell you it's a lot less than $50 or 50£.

278
00:15:04,670 --> 00:15:10,110
弗里曼: 如果我们不相信金钱所代表的价值,它们则一文不值。
Freeman: Money would be valueless if we didn't all believe in it.

279
00:15:10,110 --> 00:15:12,450
我们共同认为的现实
Our shared reality is an illusion

280
00:15:12,450 --> 00:15:14,510
其实是一个我们努力在维持的幻象,
we have to struggle to maintain.

281
00:15:14,510 --> 00:15:18,080
如果我们不严格遵守其中的规则,
And if we fail to strictly observe its rules,

282
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:21,690
现实就会轰然崩塌。
reality can crumble.

283
00:15:21,690 --> 00:15:23,790
Baggott: 一旦这些结构就这么出现在这里,
Baggott: Once these structures are out there,as it were,

284
00:15:23,790 --> 00:15:26,130
发展出属于自己的规则,
they develop,you know,laws of their own.

285
00:15:26,130 --> 00:15:28,830
发展出自己的生命,
They develop a life of their own almost.

286
00:15:28,830 --> 00:15:31,330
而对这些规则的误读,
And that misinterpreting those rules

287
00:15:31,330 --> 00:15:33,830
对规则的扭曲和改变,
and distorting those rules and changing those rules

288
00:15:33,830 --> 00:15:36,370
我们就这样将自己置于险境。
we do that at our peril.

289
00:15:36,370 --> 00:15:39,310
弗里曼: 也许没有更好的例子
Freeman: There is perhaps no greater example

290
00:15:39,310 --> 00:15:42,140
能比得上最近全球金融系统的崩溃。
than the recent near collapse of the global financial system.

291
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:43,040
[ATM机响]
[ Atm beeping ]

292
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:47,050
Baggott: 2008年全球银行业危机
Baggott: The global banking crisis of 2008

293
00:15:47,050 --> 00:15:50,380
起因就是银行家玩弄这些“游戏规则”,
resulted from bankers playing with the rules of the game.

294
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:51,720
作为结果,
And as a consequence,

295
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:55,390
金钱的价值基本一夜之间就被毁掉了。
the value of money,literally overnight,was destroyed.

296
00:15:55,390 --> 00:15:55,990
[ Bell ringing ]

297
00:15:55,990 --> 00:15:58,930
女性：华尔街在创纪录的跌幅后陷入了恐慌.
Woman:<i> Wall street is a panic after a record drop.</i>

298
00:15:58,930 --> 00:16:02,430
弗里曼: 在这短暂的时刻,人们意识到了
Freeman: For a brief moment,people became conscious

299
00:16:02,430 --> 00:16:06,400
金钱的本质只是一个幻象。
that money is essentially an illusion.

300
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:10,270
但如果我们不再相信全球货币体系,
But if we stop believing in the global monetary system,

301
00:16:10,270 --> 00:16:12,510
社会就会崩溃,
society could collapse.

302
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:16,110
所以我们选择了继续相信,
So we choose to keep on believing.

303
00:16:16,110 --> 00:16:19,010
文明也基本屈服了。
Civilization was brought almost to its knees.

304
00:16:19,010 --> 00:16:21,610
但文明并不会消失的这一事实,
But the fact that civilization didn't disappear

305
00:16:21,610 --> 00:16:23,620
也许在告诉我们这种超现实,
perhaps tells us that hyperreality,

306
00:16:23,620 --> 00:16:26,290
尽管它只是存在于我们的思维中,
despite the fact that it exists only in our minds,

307
00:16:26,290 --> 00:16:29,490
这种超现实仍难以消除。
is still too tough to kill.

308
00:16:29,490 --> 00:16:33,290
弗里曼: 为什么我们这么容易的就生活在虚幻的世界中了？
Freeman: Why is it so easy for us to live in a fantasy world?

309
00:16:33,290 --> 00:16:35,930
究竟是什么让作为人类的我们
What is it about being human

310
00:16:35,930 --> 00:16:39,930
被迫创造了这个超现实？
that compels us to create a hyperreality?

311
00:16:39,930 --> 00:16:42,500
是社会压力吗？
Is it social pressure?

312
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:43,570
[婴儿哭泣]
[ Baby crying ]

313
00:16:43,570 --> 00:16:45,810
还是我们与生俱来的？
Or is it born into us?

314
00:16:45,810 --> 00:16:49,040
这位神经科学家认为
This neuroscientist believes the answer is buried

315
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:50,910
答案就在我们脑中,
deep in our brains

316
00:16:50,910 --> 00:16:55,050
我们对现实的拒绝也许是
and our denial of reality may be essential

317
00:16:55,050 --> 00:16:59,590
我们这个物种能够生存的本质。
to the survival of our species.

318
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:04,370
人类大脑喜欢编故事,
The human brain is a storyteller.

319
00:17:04,370 --> 00:17:07,840
它告诉我们关于事物的故事,
It tells us tales about the way things are,

320
00:17:07,840 --> 00:17:12,510
这样我们就能想象事物可能会是什么样的。
and it allows us to imagine the way things could be.

321
00:17:12,510 --> 00:17:18,210
但如果我们告诉自己的故事都不是真的呢？
But what if the stories we tell ourselves aren't true?

322
00:17:18,210 --> 00:17:20,550
我们又如何知道呢？
How would we know?

323
00:17:20,550 --> 00:17:25,550
假如所有的大脑都联系起来讲述虚假的现实、
What if all our brains are wired to lie about reality

324
00:17:25,550 --> 00:17:29,060
虚假的生活场所呢？
and our place in it?

325
00:17:32,330 --> 00:17:34,530
这个人正要骑着他的摩托车
This man is about to ride his motorcycle

326
00:17:34,530 --> 00:17:37,000
穿越伦敦街头的交通堵塞。
through the traffic-clogged streets of London.

327
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:42,000
当他这么做的时候,他就会进入另一种现实之中。
When he does,he will enter an alternate reality.

328
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,800
[引擎发动]
[ Engine turns over ]

329
00:17:43,810 --> 00:17:45,510
[引擎旋转]
[ Engine revs ]

330
00:17:47,780 --> 00:17:50,450
摩托车仅占了
Motorcyclists make up less than one percent

331
00:17:50,450 --> 00:17:54,450
不足百分之一的英国交通,
of vehicle traffic in Britain.

332
00:17:54,450 --> 00:17:58,820
但却造成了总死亡及重伤人数的14%。
But they suffer 14% of total deaths and serious injuries.

333
00:17:58,820 --> 00:18:02,660
美国的骑手在车祸中也会比汽车内的人
Bikers in the U.S. are about 37 times more likely

334
00:18:02,660 --> 00:18:05,830
高出37倍的死亡率。
to die in a crash than people in a car.

335
00:18:05,830 --> 00:18:07,160
[警笛鸣叫]
[ Siren wails ]

336
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:10,800
但对于这个人来说,这些数字并不适用,
But in this man's reality,those numbers don't apply,

337
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:13,300
起码不适用于他。
at least not to him.

338
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:16,370
尽管知道这些残酷的数据,
Despite knowing the grim statistics,

