674
00:35:47,580 --> 00:35:49,040
甚至空间本身,
even space itself

675
00:35:49,040 --> 00:35:51,050
一切三维的东西
everything that's three-dimensional

676
00:35:51,050 --> 00:35:53,550
实际上都只是幻象,
is actually an illusion.

677
00:35:53,550 --> 00:35:56,690
真正的现实就是墙上的书,
The true reality is the books lining the wall.

678
00:35:56,690 --> 00:36:00,020
真相以二维的形式存在。
The true reality lives in two dimensions.

679
00:36:00,020 --> 00:36:04,130
弗里曼: 这就解释了为什么量子物体对于我们来说如此模糊,
Freeman: And this explains why quantum objects look fuzzy to us.

680
00:36:04,130 --> 00:36:05,460
它们只是投影,
They are projections

681
00:36:05,460 --> 00:36:09,730
实际并不存在于三维空间中。
that don't actually exist in three-dimensional space.

682
00:36:09,730 --> 00:36:12,470
Tong: 我们认为现在的三维世界
Tong: And what we think of as this three-dimensional world

683
00:36:12,470 --> 00:36:14,340
仅是从宇宙中的某个表面上
is just a holographic projection

684
00:36:14,340 --> 00:36:16,770
投射出来的全息影像,
from a surface somewhere in the universe

685
00:36:16,770 --> 00:36:18,210
成为了我们看到的空间。
to create the space we see.

686
00:36:18,210 --> 00:36:21,980
这样的话,柏拉图的囚犯就是正确的,
It's as if Plato's prisoners had it right all along.

687
00:36:21,980 --> 00:36:23,580
影子才是真实的,
The shadows are real.

688
00:36:23,580 --> 00:36:26,380
影子以外的都是幻影。
What's behind them was the illusion.

689
00:36:26,380 --> 00:36:29,080
弗里曼: 现在还没有办法证明
Freeman: Right now,there is no way to prove

690
00:36:29,080 --> 00:36:30,890
全息原理是否是
whether the holographic principle

691
00:36:30,890 --> 00:36:33,550
对真实的正确描述,
is the genuine description of reality

692
00:36:33,560 --> 00:36:37,330
还是理论物理学家所共同持有的错觉。
or the shared delusion of theoretical physicists.

693
00:36:37,330 --> 00:36:39,930
但也许有另一种解释,
But there may be another explanation

694
00:36:39,930 --> 00:36:41,800
来说明量子论的不可思议。
for quantum weirdness.

695
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:44,770
真实如此模糊的原因
What if reality gets blurry

696
00:36:44,770 --> 00:36:47,640
是因为它从未存在过吗？
because it was never there to begin with?

697
00:36:47,640 --> 00:36:49,470
一些科学家认为
Some scientists say

698
00:36:49,470 --> 00:36:54,410
现实是一个故意创造的幻象。
our reality could be a deliberately created illusion.

699
00:36:58,000 --> 00:37:00,330
通过科学的工具,
Using the tools of science,

700
00:37:00,330 --> 00:37:04,730
我们只能一瞥这巨大结构的一小部分,
we catch glimpses of the vast structure of creation.

701
00:37:04,730 --> 00:37:08,400
有太多的我们无法看到,
There is so much we cannot see.

702
00:37:08,410 --> 00:37:12,710
为什么找出真相如此困难？
Why is the truth so hard to find?

703
00:37:12,710 --> 00:37:17,010
也许是因为我们生存的宇宙
Perhaps it's because the universe we live in

704
00:37:17,010 --> 00:37:21,250
只是一个更大真实的一小部分...
is just a small part of a larger reality...

705
00:37:21,250 --> 00:37:28,430
我们都只生活在梦中的世界,
And we are all just living in a world of dreams.

706
00:37:30,630 --> 00:37:35,670
[闹钟响]
[ Alarm blaring ]

707
00:37:35,670 --> 00:37:36,700
[哔,响声停止]
[ Alarm beeps,blaring stops ]

708
00:37:36,700 --> 00:37:39,640
你是否做过递归梦...
Have you ever had a recursive dream...

709
00:37:39,640 --> 00:37:40,800
[闹钟响]
[ Alarm blaring ]

710
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:41,940
[哔,响声停止]
[ Alarm beeps,blaring stops ]

711
00:37:41,940 --> 00:37:45,210
...就是梦中有梦又有梦？
...a dream with a dream within a dream?

712
00:37:45,210 --> 00:37:48,650
[闹钟响]
[ Alarm blaring ]

713
00:37:48,650 --> 00:37:49,980
[哔,响声停止]
[ Alarm beeps,blaring stops ]

714
00:37:49,980 --> 00:37:53,820
Jan Westerhoff就做过,
Jan Westerhoff has.

715
00:37:53,820 --> 00:37:57,220
根据他所知道的,他可能还在梦中,
And for all he knows,he might still be dreaming.

716
00:37:57,220 --> 00:38:00,560
或者你现在正在梦着这些。
Or you might be dreaming this.

717
00:38:00,560 --> 00:38:03,830
Westerhoff: 你如何知道今天早上你醒来
Westerhoff: How do you know whether waking up this morning

718
00:38:03,830 --> 00:38:05,230
是真正的清醒？
was actually a real awakening?

719
00:38:05,230 --> 00:38:09,000
也许你只是从另一个梦中醒来。
Perhaps you just woke up into another dream.

720
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:11,070
你应该对此担心的原因
The reason why you should worry about this

721
00:38:11,070 --> 00:38:13,300
正是因为有很大的可能性表明
is that there is actually a significant chance

722
00:38:13,300 --> 00:38:15,470
我们现在正在做梦。
that we are dreaming right now.

723
00:38:15,470 --> 00:38:17,370
我们来算一下。
Let's do the numbers.

724
00:38:17,370 --> 00:38:19,610
弗里曼: 根据Jan的说法,
Freeman: According to Jan,

725
00:38:19,610 --> 00:38:24,720
大多数人每天需要8小时睡眠,16个小时处于清醒状态。
most people spend 8 hours asleep and 16 hours awake every day.

726
00:38:24,720 --> 00:38:29,050
睡眠中大约有20%的时间处于
About 20% of sleep is spent in the r.E.M. State,

727
00:38:29,050 --> 00:38:30,550
快速眼动睡眠期,
when you dream.

728
00:38:30,550 --> 00:38:35,020
8的20%,就是1.6,这表示...
20% of 8 is 1.6,which means...

729
00:38:35,020 --> 00:38:37,560
Westerhoff: 我们知道在这个时期中,
Westerhoff: We know that,at this very moment,

730
00:38:37,560 --> 00:38:40,400
此时你有十分之一的机会正在做梦,
you have a 1 in 10 chance of dreaming right now,

731
00:38:40,400 --> 00:38:43,300
这的确是一个很高的可能性。
which is actually quite a significant probability.

732
00:38:47,140 --> 00:38:50,610
弗里曼: Jan其实也并不相信自己生活在梦境,
Freeman: Jan doesn't actually believe he lives in a dreamworld,

733
00:38:50,610 --> 00:38:54,610
但作为英格兰杜伦大学的哲学家,
but as a philosopher at the University of Durham in England,

734
00:38:54,610 --> 00:39:00,050
他的工作就是对事物为什么是这样进行提问。
his job is to question how and why things are the way they are.

735
00:39:00,050 --> 00:39:03,520
不论概率数字是多少,
And despite what the numbers say,

736
00:39:03,520 --> 00:39:08,860
逻辑会告诉你你可能并不是在睡觉。
logic tells you you are probably not asleep.

737
00:39:08,860 --> 00:39:10,360
如果这是梦境,
If this was a dreamworld,

738
00:39:10,360 --> 00:39:13,130
为什么会被因果关系所束缚？
why would it be bound by the laws of causality?

739
00:39:13,130 --> 00:39:16,570
为什么狂暴的火龙不会来到伦敦,
Why don't fire-breathing dragons go rampaging through London,

740
00:39:16,570 --> 00:39:18,840
摧毁这座城市？
destroying the city?

741
00:39:22,670 --> 00:39:24,370
好吧,这是不可能的。
Well,they don't.

742
00:39:24,370 --> 00:39:26,710
你看到的都只是幻象。
What you saw was just an illusion.

743
00:39:26,710 --> 00:39:28,680
现实要遵守一系列严格的规则,
Reality follows a strict set of rules,

744
00:39:28,680 --> 00:39:31,480
即使在量子层面会有些模糊。
even though it gets a little blurry at the quantum level.

745
00:39:31,480 --> 00:39:32,820
这又如何解释呢？
What might explain that?

746
00:39:32,820 --> 00:39:35,220
也许我们生活在由高层次现实
Well,perhaps we are living in a simulation

747
00:39:35,220 --> 00:39:37,320
模拟的真实中。
made by a higher-order reality.

748
00:39:38,790 --> 00:39:41,860
弗里曼: 换句话说,现实可能并不是梦境,
Freeman: In other words,reality may not be a dream,

749
00:39:41,860 --> 00:39:44,230
但很可能是一种计算机模拟。
but it could be a computer simulation.

750
00:39:46,330 --> 00:39:49,430
想象这么一个时间,也许从现在开始几个世纪后,
Imagine a time,perhaps centuries from now,

751
00:39:49,430 --> 00:39:51,270
当我们的后代有能力
when our descendants have the power

752
00:39:51,270 --> 00:39:55,610
用计算机构建人脑全部功能的模型时,
to model fully functional human brains in computers.

753
00:39:55,610 --> 00:39:58,070
这些模拟的思维就存在于
These simulated minds could be placed

754
00:39:58,070 --> 00:40:00,240
计算机模拟世界中,
in computer-simulated worlds,

755
00:40:00,240 --> 00:40:03,280
也许甚至可以重建过去。
perhaps even re-creations of the past.

756
00:40:03,280 --> 00:40:06,420
他们永远不会知道他们并不是真实的。
They would never know they weren't real.

757
00:40:06,420 --> 00:40:09,450
假如这一切早已发生了呢？
What if this has already happened?

758
00:40:09,450 --> 00:40:14,290
Westerhoff: 我们如何知道我们所处的当代
Westerhoff: How do we know that the present year we are in here

759
00:40:14,290 --> 00:40:18,630
的确是真实的,而不是过去的重放,
is actually the original rather than some sort of rerun

760
00:40:18,630 --> 00:40:22,330
真实过去发生的那些奇怪事件可能已经被修改,
where some weird event in the past had been changed

761
00:40:22,330 --> 00:40:25,700
成为了我们现在看到的过去真实的分枝？
just to see what kind of ramifications it had?

762
00:40:29,410 --> 00:40:32,070
弗里曼: 无论你是否相信,
Freeman: Believe it or not,

763
00:40:32,080 --> 00:40:37,450
有这么一个几率表明,我们都是这个巨型模拟中的一部分。
there is a chance we are all part of a giant simulation.

764
00:40:37,450 --> 00:40:40,480
想象一下,比如说,我买到了一幅达利的画,
Imagine,for example,that I buy a dalí print.

765
00:40:40,480 --> 00:40:42,490
我很激动,
I get really excited about this

766
00:40:42,490 --> 00:40:45,090
因为我很喜欢里面融软的钟。
because I just love melting clocks.

767
00:40:45,090 --> 00:40:48,220
现在问题就是根据专业人士判断,
Now the problem here is that,according to experts,

768
00:40:48,220 --> 00:40:51,600
市场上约90%达利的画都是假的。
about 90% of all dalí prints on the market are fake.

769
00:40:51,600 --> 00:40:55,830
所以我的这幅画是假的的概率为0.9。
So the chance that I've got a fake here is 0.9.

770
00:40:55,830 --> 00:40:57,170
嗯？
Huh?

771
00:40:57,170 --> 00:41:00,500
弗里曼: 我们的世界有多大的可能性是假的呢？
Freeman: What are the odds that our world is a fake?

772
00:41:01,670 --> 00:41:04,710
有人说高达二十分之一,
Some say as high as 1 in 20.

773
00:41:04,710 --> 00:41:08,150
但Jan认为可能性并不重要,
But Jan says the percentage isn't important.

774
00:41:08,150 --> 00:41:12,180
如果你有可能是被模拟出来的,
If there is any chance at all that you are simulated,

775
00:41:12,180 --> 00:41:15,220
那么你就不能排除
then you can't dismiss the possibility

776
00:41:15,220 --> 00:41:18,190
你就是被模拟出来的。
that you<i> are</i> simulated.

777
00:41:18,190 --> 00:41:19,760
但问题就在这儿,
But here is the thing

778
00:41:19,760 --> 00:41:23,030
就算一切都是梦,又有什么关系呢？
even if this is all a dream,does it really matter?

779
00:41:23,030 --> 00:41:24,860
即使这是一块梦中的蛋糕,
Even if this is just a dream cake

780
00:41:24,860 --> 00:41:30,100
我用梦中的钱买下了它,它尝起来仍然很不错。
and I paid for it with dream money,it still tastes great.

781
00:41:30,100 --> 00:41:33,440
假定这一切都顺理成章,
So presupposing this all continues,

782
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:36,570
那么是梦还是模拟还有什么关系吗？
does it really matter whether it's a dream or a simulation?

783
00:41:36,570 --> 00:41:39,580
我仍然能规划我的生活,因产生果,
I can still plan my life,causes will have effects,

784
00:41:39,580 --> 00:41:43,080
做出行为就造成结果。
and actions will have consequences.

785
00:41:49,720 --> 00:41:53,820
现实是真实的吗？
Is reality real?

786
00:41:53,820 --> 00:41:57,160
看起来当然是真实的。
It certainly seems real to us.

787
00:41:57,160 --> 00:41:59,960
但现在我们知道,我们所感知到的现实
But we now know the reality we perceive

788
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:03,500
仅仅只是真实的一小部分。
is just a small slice of what really is.

789
00:42:03,500 --> 00:42:07,800
可能最终这不重要,
And,perhaps,in the long run,that doesn't matter.

790
00:42:07,800 --> 00:42:12,640
对我们来说最重要的是我们所知晓的那部分真实。
What matters most to us is the reality we know.

791
00:42:12,640 --> 00:42:17,150
正如哲学家皇帝马可·奥勒留两千年前所写的,
As the philosopher-king Marcus Aurelius wrote 2,000 years ago,

792
00:42:17,150 --> 00:42:21,420
“宇宙是变化的,
"The universe is change.

793
00:42:21,420 --> 00:42:25,920
我们的生活取决于我们心态。”
Our life is what our thoughts make it."

